    id: "why-we-waste", group: "Understanding isrof || Isrofni tushunish",
    title: "Why do people waste? || Nega odamlar isrof qiladi?",
    summary: "Seven roots of waste, from not knowing the religion to copying others, and how to pull each one out. || Isrofning yetti ildizi: dinni bilmaslikdan tortib boshqalarga taqlid qilishgacha, va har birini qanday sug‘urib tashlash.",
    sources: [B("Isrofning sabablari"), "Quran 17:29", "Quran 56:41–45", "Abu Dawud 4833", "Tirmidhi 2378"],
    blocks: [
      P("To stop waste, we have to know where it comes from. The book names seven causes. Most of us will recognise at least one of them in ourselves. || Isrofni to‘xtatish uchun uning qayerdan kelishini bilishimiz kerak. Kitobda yetti sabab sanalgan. Ko‘pchiligimiz o‘zimizda ulardan kamida bittasini topamiz."),
      L("The seven causes || Yetti sabab", [
        "1. Not knowing the religion. Without knowledge, a person does not see waste as a sin with consequences in this world and the next. || 1. Dinni bilmaslik. Ilmsiz odam isrofni bu dunyo va oxiratda oqibati bor gunoh deb bilmaydi.",
        "2. Growing up in waste. A child raised in a wasteful home thinks waste is normal and copies the adults. || 2. Bolalikdan isrofda o‘sish. Isrofchi oilada o‘sgan bola isrofni oddiy hol deb biladi va kattalarga ergashadi.",
        "3. Forgetting that life changes. Plenty can turn into hunger and wealth into poverty; the wise save in good times. || 3. Dunyo o‘zgaruvchan ekanini unutish. To‘qlik ochlikka, boylik kambag‘allikka aylanishi mumkin; oqil odam yaxshi kunda jamg‘aradi.",
        "4. Moving from hardship to ease. Some say, “We were patient long enough, now let us enjoy”, and spend wildly, which can bring the hardship back. || 4. Qiyinchilikdan osonchilikka chiqish. Ba’zilar: “Vaqtida sabr qilganmiz, endi maza qilib yashaylik”, deb isrofga o‘tadi va bu qiyinchilikni qaytarishi mumkin.",
        "5. Wasteful friends. “A man is upon the religion of his friend, so let each of you look at whom he befriends” (Abu Dawud 4833; Tirmidhi 2378). || 5. Isrofchilar bilan do‘stlik. “Kishi do‘stining dinidadir. Biringiz kimga do‘st bo‘lishiga nazar solsin” (Abu Dovud 4833; Termiziy 2378).",
        "6. Loving praise and fame. Some spend to look generous and be talked about. || 6. Manmanlik va shuhratparastlik. Ba’zilar saxiy ko‘rinish va gap-so‘z bo‘lish uchun sarflaydi.",
        "7. Copying others. “So-and-so did this, so I must do more.” The book calls this one of the biggest causes of waste today. || 7. Boshqalarga taqlid qilish. “Falonchi shunday qilibdi, men undan o‘tkazishim kerak.” Kitob buni bugungi isrofning eng katta sabablaridan biri deydi.",
      ]),
      Q("Do not tie your hand to your neck, nor stretch it out completely, or you will sit blamed and full of regret. || Qo‘lingni bo‘yningga bog‘lab olma. Uni bir yo‘la yozib ham yuborma. Yana malomat va hasratda o‘tirib qolmagin.", "Quran 17:29"),
      P("This verse draws two pictures. The miser has tied his hand to his neck so he can never reach his purse. The waster has opened his hand so wide that everything falls out. Both end up blamed and full of regret. The way of Islam is the middle. || Bu oyatda ikki surat chizilgan. Baxil qo‘lini bo‘yniga bog‘lab olgan, hamyoniga qo‘l cho‘za olmaydi. Isrofchi qo‘lini shunchalik yozib yuborganki, bor narsasi to‘kilib ketadi. Ikkisi ham malomat va hasratda qoladi. Islom yo‘li — o‘rtacha yo‘l."),
      L("The end of waste in the next life || Isrofning oxiratdagi oqibati", [
        "Allah describes the “people of the left” in scorching wind, boiling water and the shade of black smoke (56:41–44). || Alloh “chap taraf egalari”ni olovli shamol, qaynoq suv va qop-qora tutun soyasida deb vasf qiladi (56:41–44).",
        "Then He gives the reason: “Before this they were living in luxury” (56:45), chasing pleasure and forgetting faith. || So‘ng sababini aytadi: “Albatta, ular bundan oldin maishatparast edilar” (56:45), lazzat ortidan quvib, iymonni unutgan edilar.",
        "ʿUmar said: “Do not be slaves of your stomachs. It ruins the body, brings illness and keeps you from prayer. Be moderate; moderation is better for the body.” (reported) || Umar: “Taom va ichimlikda qorin bandasi bo‘lmanglar. Bu jasadni buzadi, kasal keltiradi, namozdan qoldiradi. Tejamkor bo‘linglar, bu jasad uchun yaxshi”, deganlar (rivoyat).",
      ]),
      { type: "scenario", id: "israf-cause-copy", situation: "Your cousin had a huge birthday party with a hired hall. Your family can afford something small. A relative says: “If you do less, people will talk.” What is the best answer? || Amakivachchangizga zal ijaraga olinib, katta tug‘ilgan kun o‘tkazildi. Oilangizning imkoni kichikrog‘iga yetadi. Bir qarindoshingiz: “Kamroq qilsangiz, odamlar gapiradi”, deydi. Eng to‘g‘ri javob qaysi?",
        options: [
          { text: "Borrow money so ours is bigger. || Qarz olib, biznikini kattaroq qilamiz.", feedback: "Spending beyond your means to beat others is exactly the copying the book warns about. || Boshqalardan o‘tish uchun imkondan ortiq sarflash — kitob ogohlantirgan taqlidning aynan o‘zi." },
          { text: "Do something simple and warm that fits what we have, and maybe give something to someone in need. || O‘z imkonimizga yarasha sodda va samimiy narsa qilamiz, balki muhtojga ham biror narsa beramiz.", best: true, feedback: "Moderation, sincerity and generosity, without competing. || Musobaqasiz, mo‘tadillik, ixlos va saxovat." },
          { text: "Cancel everything and stay angry. || Hammasini bekor qilib, xafa bo‘lib yuramiz.", feedback: "Joy within limits is good; the problem is the competition, not the celebration. || Me’yordagi xursandchilik yaxshi; muammo bayramda emas, musobaqada." },
        ] },
      { type: "reflect", think: ["Which of the seven causes do I see most in myself? || Yetti sababdan qaysi birini o‘zimda ko‘proq ko‘raman?", "Do I ever buy something mainly so others will see it? || Biror narsani asosan boshqalar ko‘rsin deb sotib olganmanmi?"],
        home: ["Before buying something big, ask together: Do we need it? Can we afford it? Would we buy it if no one saw it? || Katta narsa olishdan oldin birga so‘rang: Bu bizga kerakmi? Imkonimiz bormi? Hech kim ko‘rmasa ham olarmidik?"] },
      L("Key takeaways || Asosiy xulosalar", [
        "Knowing the causes of waste is the first step to ending it. || Isrof sabablarini bilish uni tugatishning birinchi qadami.",
        "Ignorance, upbringing, forgetting that life changes, sudden ease, friends, love of fame and copying others all lead to waste. || Bilmaslik, tarbiya, dunyo o‘zgaruvchanligini unutish, to‘satdan kenglik, do‘stlar, shuhratparastlik va taqlid isrofga olib boradi.",
        "Islam’s way is the middle: neither a tied hand nor an emptied one. || Islom yo‘li — o‘rtacha: na bog‘langan qo‘l, na bo‘shab qolgan qo‘l.",
      ]),
    ],
    quiz: [
      { q: "Why does a person who does not know the religion waste more easily? || Nega dinni bilmagan odam osonroq isrof qiladi?", options: ["He does not see it as a sin with consequences || U buni oqibati bor gunoh deb bilmaydi", "He is richer || U boyroq", "He has more time || Uning vaqti ko‘proq", "He never eats || U hech ovqat yemaydi"], answer: 0, why: "Knowledge shows the reality and end of waste. || Ilm isrofning haqiqati va oqibatini ko‘rsatadi.", src: B("Isrofning sabablari") },
      { q: "What happens to a child raised in a wasteful home? || Isrofchi oilada o‘sgan bolaga nima bo‘ladi?", options: ["He hates waste || U isrofni yomon ko‘radi", "He thinks waste is normal and copies it || Isrofni oddiy hol deb, unga ergashadi", "Nothing || Hech narsa", "He becomes a miser || Baxil bo‘ladi"], answer: 1, why: "Children copy what they see. || Bolalar ko‘rganiga ergashadi.", src: B("Isrofning sabablari") },
      { q: "What does 17:29 compare the miser to? || 17:29-oyat baxilni nimaga o‘xshatadi?", options: ["A bird || Qushga", "Someone whose hand is tied to his neck || Qo‘li bo‘yniga bog‘langan kishiga", "A river || Daryoga", "A king || Podshohga"], answer: 1, why: "He cannot reach his purse to give. || U berish uchun hamyoniga qo‘l cho‘za olmaydi.", src: "Quran 17:29" },
      { q: "What happens to the one who stretches his hand out completely? || Qo‘lini butunlay yozib yuborgan kishiga nima bo‘ladi?", options: ["He becomes famous || Mashhur bo‘ladi", "He sits blamed and full of regret || Malomat va hasratda o‘tirib qoladi", "He gets richer || Boyib ketadi", "Nothing || Hech narsa"], answer: 1, why: "Both extremes end in regret. || Ikki chekka ham pushaymonlik bilan tugaydi.", src: "Quran 17:29" },
      { q: "What should a wise person do in times of plenty? || Oqil odam to‘kinchilik paytida nima qilishi kerak?", options: ["Spend it all quickly || Hammasini tez sarflab yuborish", "Remember life changes and save for harder days || Dunyo o‘zgarishini eslab, og‘ir kunlar uchun jamg‘arish", "Stop working || Ishlashni to‘xtatish", "Borrow more || Ko‘proq qarz olish"], answer: 1, why: "Plenty can turn into hardship. || To‘qlik ochlikka aylanishi mumkin.", src: B("Isrofning sabablari") },
      { q: "“A man is upon the religion of his…” || “Kishi … dinidadir.”", options: ["…father || …otasining", "…friend || …do‘stining", "…teacher || …ustozining", "…neighbour || …qo‘shnisining"], answer: 1, why: "So look at whom you befriend. || Shuning uchun kimga do‘st bo‘lishingizga qarang.", src: "Abu Dawud 4833" },
      { q: "Which cause does the book call one of the biggest today? || Kitob qaysi sababni bugungi kunning eng kattalaridan biri deydi?", options: ["Copying others and competing || Boshqalarga taqlid va musobaqa", "Eating dates || Xurmo yeyish", "Saving money || Pul jamg‘arish", "Reading books || Kitob o‘qish"], answer: 0, why: "“So-and-so did it, I must do more.” || “Falonchi shunday qilibdi, men undan o‘tkazaman.”", src: B("Isrofning sabablari") },
      { q: "Why were the “people of the left” punished, according to 56:45? || 56:45-oyatga ko‘ra “chap taraf egalari” nega azoblanadi?", options: ["They lived in luxury, chasing pleasure || Ular maishatparast edilar, lazzat ortidan quvdilar", "They were poor || Ular kambag‘al edilar", "They travelled a lot || Ko‘p safar qilgandilar", "They worked hard || Qattiq mehnat qildilar"], answer: 0, why: "“Before this they were living in luxury.” || “Albatta, ular bundan oldin maishatparast edilar.”", src: "Quran 56:45" },
      { q: "What did ʿUmar say overeating does? || Umar ko‘p yeyish nima qiladi, degan?", options: ["Makes you stronger || Kuchliroq qiladi", "Ruins the body, brings illness and keeps you from prayer || Jasadni buzadi, kasal keltiradi, namozdan qoldiradi", "Nothing || Hech narsa", "Makes you clever || Aqlli qiladi"], answer: 1, why: "Moderation is better for the body. || Tejamkorlik jasad uchun yaxshi.", src: "ʿUmar (reported)" },
      { q: "Spending to look generous and be praised comes from… || Saxiy ko‘rinish va maqtov uchun sarflash nimadan?", options: ["Love of fame and showing off || Shuhratparastlik va manmanlikdan", "Sincerity || Ixlosdan", "Zakat || Zakotdan", "Gratitude || Shukrdan"], answer: 0, why: "One of the seven causes of waste. || Isrofning yetti sababidan biri.", src: B("Isrofning sabablari") },
    ],
  },
];
